Track 3: Ivory Label, Red Pencil
- Story & Context: Before a performance, Rui writes the set order on removable ivory labels attached to the corridor switchboard. Tiago changes the sequence at the last minute and marks the revision with red pencil instead of replacing the labels. The visual mismatch becomes the basis of the track’s arrangement: fixed drone underneath constantly revised rhythmic blocks.

The opening uses only gaida, one cimbalom dyad, and bass-clarinet breath. Every time Tiago introduces a new kuduro pattern, Zsófia shifts the cimbalom attack by one subdivision while Milena keeps the same drone unchanged. Rui alternates dry key clicks with long low tones, acting like punctuation between revisions.

The climax arrives when three different drum patterns are cycled in rapid succession without changing tempo or harmony. The final sound is not a fade but the dry click of a label being peeled from the switchboard while the gaida drone cuts only after the ensemble has fully stopped.
